{"id": "q0059", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2950035881, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "0c0eb5f5089b4570f4b5f593318ef7c0c5f8ba06a58bdaf93a6686b9afa1d86e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 7, "query": "Tom found 214 seashells, Nancy found 432 seashells, and Benny found 86 seashells on the beach. When they cleaned them, they discovered that 67 were cracked. How many good seashells did they find together?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0059.wav", "input_sha256": "4b7aba3e715ca6c96d897631547361b3fbd6ebf5487bb3d39deeac47e9cc3f7c", "input_samples": 284600, "input_s": 17.788, "n_real_chunks": 18, "score": 0.2542, "act": 0.9962, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, let's figure this out. First, we add up all the seashells they found: Tom's 2 14, Nancy' s 43 2, and Benny' s 86. So, 2 14 plus 4 32 is 6 4 6, then adding 86 gives us 7 32 total seashell s. Next, we subtract the cracked ones: 7 3 2 minus 6 7 equal s 6 6 5 good sea shells. So, together they found 665 good sea shells.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 17, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 35, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0059_balanced_local.wav", "sha256": "f7b2bf1d5bea75335e004f4e7ddc4bbd62b61300f5965564905d7575c75c4354", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 35.0}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.077, 1.135, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.078, 2.138, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.08, 3.14, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.076,