{"id": "q0073", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2100720181, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "0c0eb5f5089b4570f4b5f593318ef7c0c5f8ba06a58bdaf93a6686b9afa1d86e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 7, "query": "Jackie grew 3\" over the summer.  She is now 2\" shorter than Anne, who is twice the size of Albert.  If Albert is 36\" tall, how tall was Jackie before summer?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0073.wav", "input_sha256": "561b9b4bbd5759fa5d23f4d63067fb11f2e84a6df7b09710ff4d4144d8abb3d3", "input_samples": 214000, "input_s": 13.375, "n_real_chunks": 14, "score": 0.1231, "act": 0.9988, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Albert is 3 6 inches tall, so Anne must be twice his size, or 7 2 inches. Jack ie is two inches shorter than Anne, making her 7 0 inches tall after the summer. Since she grew three inches over the summer, we can subtract that from her current height to find her height before the summer growth. So, 7 0 minus 3 equals 6 7 inches. Therefore, Jackie was 6 7 inches tall before summer.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 13, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 26, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0073_balanced_local.wav", "sha256": "455e3b1aff51a3c38458c90095f136f036363ee31a3d0a4a080ebd5234e1498a", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 26.2}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.075, 1.134, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.074, 2.136, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.076, 3.135, 1, 0, 0], [